# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  debug_meta.la — the literal self-application, run BY HAND.
#
#  ── WHY THIS IS NOT IN THE GATE, and the number that decided it ─────
#  CLAUDE.md's Debugging Principle asks for Meta-Debug(Meta-Debug) =
#  Debug, and debug_eval.la's header claims it is "the evaluator watching
#  itself". This file is that claim taken literally: DEBUG_EVAL tracing
#  eval.la's own RUN as it evaluates a program.
#
#  It is not gated because it was MEASURED, not guessed: past 150 seconds
#  on the host, before the host==VM half doubles it. Slice 12's budget
#  bounds what is EMITTED, not what is EXECUTED — the whole meta-
#  evaluation still runs, so a budget cannot make this cheap. That is a
#  property of the thing, not a defect in it.
#
#  The gated check (debug 14) traces a small evaluator instead — an
#  honest level below this one, affordable at ~11s, asserting the same
#  shape: a fixed point built, a term dispatched, the answer unchanged.
#
#  ── RUN IT ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#      ./tiny_host debug_meta.la
#  Expect minutes, and a trace bounded to the budget below. Raise the
#  budget to see more; the run time does not change with it.
#
#  This follows the project's existing precedent for expensive capstones
#  (theourgia_*_live.la, sigil_live.la): the gate verifies the affordable
#  core, the capstone is run by hand and documented.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

#   Imports the DEBUGGER, not a copy of it. Slice 13 gave debug_eval.la an
#   export list for exactly this: a capstone that duplicated the machinery
#   would be testing its own copy, which is the drift hazard that whole file
#   exists to watch.
import("debug_eval.la")

#   The object program IS an evaluator: it imports eval.la and calls RUN
#   on a program it parses at run time. Tracing it therefore traces the
#   self-hosted parser AND the self-hosted evaluator, which is what makes
#   it expensive and also what makes it the literal claim.
glyph SRC_SELF = "import(\"eval.la\")\nglyph MAIN = RUN_GLYPH(\"X\")(PARSE_PROGRAM(\"glyph X = concat(\\\"a\\\")(\\\"b\\\")\"))"

glyph MAIN = SEQ(SEQ(
    print("--- meta capstone: DEBUG_EVAL tracing eval.la's own evaluator ---"))(
    print(AGREES_BUD(40)(SRC_SELF))))(
    print("--- meta capstone: end (agreement above is the assertion) ---"))
